From: SM-G955N Ubuntu port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] libhybris: honor gralloc1 allocated/imported handle ownership

The gralloc1 release contract requires manual close/delete without the release-
implies-delete capability only for handles not allocated locally. The original
S8 gralloc1 capability callback advertises layered buffers only; its release
callback deletes locally allocated final references itself. Unconditional manual
close/delete therefore accesses an already deleted handle. Distinguish local and
imported ownership, retain advertised capability behavior and preserve errors.
No global vendor quirk, fake return, or unsupported capability is introduced.
Original upstream notices are retained.

--- a/hybris/gralloc/gralloc.c
+++ b/hybris/gralloc/gralloc.c
@@ -250,9 +250,11 @@
     ) else if GRALLOC1(
         ret = gralloc1_release(gralloc1_device, handle);
 
-        // this needs to happen if the last reference is gone, this function is
-        // only called in such cases.
-        if (!gralloc1_release_implies_delete) {
+        /* gralloc1.h release(): without RELEASE_IMPLY_DELETE, the caller
+         * closes/deletes only imported handles. Locally allocated handles
+         * are owned by the HAL, which releases them itself. On an error no
+         * ownership transfer was established, so leave the handle intact. */
+        if (ret == 0 && !gralloc1_release_implies_delete && !was_allocated) {
             native_handle_close((native_handle_t*)handle);
             native_handle_delete((native_handle_t*)handle);
         }
